From a0c63eb67bc3f02b84b3d547ce310d6723372bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yankneck696 <yankneck696@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:57:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Two-tone test signal on TUNE, and a movable TRANSMIT window

Split out of #743 at the maintainer's suggestion, with the fixes from that
review. Independent of the PlutoSDR work: it needs no particular radio.

A 2T chip beside TUNE transmits 700 Hz and 1900 Hz together at the tune
level until clicked again, like the Tone button other SDR programs have:
the signal amplifier linearity is judged with, and the one a predistorter
learns from, since a steady carrier has a single amplitude. TxState gains
two_tone and Command gains SetTuneTwoTone; wire protocol v212, the one bump
for this change. Keying and level are TUNE's own, so every guard on TUNE
applies. The 2T chip's label and hover text are new messages, in en-US and
translated into the other ten languages.

From the review:

- Two-tone ends with the TUNE it was chosen for. Only the main window's
  chips send SetTuneTwoTone; the footswitch and hotkey, rigctld's TUNE,
  TCI's tune:, remote clients and a headless tune send a bare
  SetTune(true), which means a carrier, and after one 2T over they keyed a
  two-tone instead. It is now cleared wherever TUNE ends: SetTune(false)
  (the tune time limit goes through it), a switch to a receive-only mode,
  and a refused key-up. A new engine test keys a 2T over and then a bare
  TUNE, and checks the second is a carrier.
- The sideband is the transmit dial's (is_lower_sideband_at), so SSTV and
  RADE send it in the lower sideband on 160/80/40 m as they do their
  traffic.
- The recording tap heard TUNE's 1 kHz tone while the two-tone was on the
  air. It now hears the two tones, taken from the same step of the same
  phases as the transmitted samples.

On the compact strip the TX chip's drop-down hung over the S-meter, which is
what an operator watches while setting drive and tune. It now opens a
TRANSMIT window instead: the same controls, draggable clear of the meter,
and open through an over until closed.
